.TH LOWPASSFILTER 1
.SH NAME
lowpassfilter \- four ways to draw the same step response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/lowpassfilter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I LowPassFilter
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/LowPassFilter.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A blue square wave, then the same first-order step response four times
over, a keypress apart.  Cyan is the closed-form exponential.  Black is
the one-line recurrence everybody writes, y = 0.99y + 0.01x, which lands
on the same curve only because the step happens to be one every sample.
Red is the kernel's own filter, which takes the step length as an
argument and so gives the same answer when the steps are ragged \- and
here they are random lengths, which is the point.  Green is that filter
ten times faster, to show what the coefficient means.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Add the next curve; the last exits
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/lowpassfilter.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
